From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] string: Add wcslen() for newer Rust core

Newer Rust core (CStr/OsStr helpers) references wcslen(); provide a
minimal implementation so m1n1 links with current nightly toolchains.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/src/string.c b/src/string.c
index 8681be3..ca1318a 100644
--- a/src/string.c
+++ b/src/string.c
@@ -231,3 +231,12 @@ long atol(const char *s)
 
     return val;
 }
+
+/* Referenced by newer Rust core (CStr/OsStr helpers) */
+size_t wcslen(const int *s)
+{
+    size_t n = 0;
+    while (s[n])
+        n++;
+    return n;
+}
